## Why This Is Asked
Tests serverless performance and cold-start behavior, a common real-world pain point with fine-grained scaling and per-invocation costs.

## Key Concepts
- Serverless latency composition (API Gateway, Lambda cold/warm, S3 I/O)
- Cold-start measurement and provisioning strategies
- Burst/load ramps and ramp-rate effects
- Isolating components in a testing context

## Code Example
```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
export default function() {
  http.post('https://api.example.com/resize', JSON.stringify({ key: 'test.jpg' }), { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }});
  sleep(0.5);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify cold-start impact across regions?
- What changes to test would you make if responses must be <200ms end-to-end with 99th percentile guarantee?

